  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Gender and Christianity in Modern Europe (2012), published by Leuven University Press, has been cited 5 times. Beyond that, it has been downloaded 3,876 times.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Gender and Christianity in Modern Europe by Patrick Pasture was published by Leuven University Press in 2012. Conceptually, the work connects to Feminization (sociology), Masculinity, Christianity, Gender studies and Sociology.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">OpenAlex records 5 citations. Citations peaked in 2018 with 3 citing works. Notable citing venues include Mortality, Central European History and The British Journal of Social Work. The citing works include 3 journal articles and 1 book chapter. They come from 4 countries, led by Belgium, the United Kingdom and Poland.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">It has been downloaded 3,876 times via OAPEN. Its subject matter aligns with Gender equality among the Sustainable Development Goals.</p>",
